<section class="framework-section bg-white">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row">
      
      <!-- Left Column: Title and Intro -->
      <div class="col-left">
        <h2 class="section-title">High Conviction in Construction. <span class="text-highlight">Discipline</span> in Risk.</h2>
        <p class="font-secondary intro-text">
          We believe concentrated portfolios can create greater value when conviction is supported by a rigorous framework. Our portfolios are constructed around our highest-conviction ideas, while clearly defined risk parameters ensure that conviction remains disciplined.
        </p>
      </div>
      
      <!-- Right Column: Framework Details -->
      <div class="col-right">
        <div class="architecture-list">
          
          <div class="architecture-item">
            <div class="item-number font-secondary">01</div>
            <div class="item-content">
              <h4>Built Around Conviction</h4>
              <ul class="framework-list font-secondary">
                <li><strong>Concentrated Portfolio -</strong> Designed to allocate capital meaningfully to our strongest investment ideas.</li>
                <li><strong>Stock and Sector Limits -</strong> Position sizes are established with discipline. Exposure is carefully managed to avoid excessive concentration risk</li>
                <li><strong>Typically fully invested -</strong> Keep capital productively deployed and minimizing unnecessary cash drag</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
          
          <div class="architecture-item">
            <div class="item-number font-secondary">02</div>
            <div class="item-content">
              <h4>Discipline Through the Investment Cycle</h4>
              <p class="font-secondary mb-3">Risk management is embedded in every stage of the investment process not treated as an afterthought.</p>
              <ul class="framework-list font-secondary">
                <li><strong>Liquidity awareness -</strong> To ensure positions remain appropriate as portfolios evolve.</li>
                <li><strong>Active rebalancing -</strong> Reassessed as investment theses, valuations, fundamentals, and risk parameters change.</li>
                <li><strong>Continuous monitoring -</strong> Evaluate company-specific developments and broader market factors that may affect portfolio risk.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
          
        </div>
      </div>
      
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style lang="scss">
  .framework-section {
    padding: 8rem 0;
    background-color: #f8f9fa; /* Very light grey/white background */
  }
  
  .row {
    display: flex;
    gap: 6rem;
    
    @media (max-width: 992px) {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 3rem;
    }
  }
  
  .col-left {
    flex: 1;
    max-width: 450px;
    position: sticky;
    top: 120px;
    align-self: flex-start;
    
    @media (max-width: 992px) {
      max-width: 100%;
      position: relative;
      top: 0;
    }
  }
  
  .col-right {
    flex: 1.5;
  }
  
  .section-title {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 4vw, 3.5rem);
    font-weight: 300;
    line-height: 1.2;
    color: #000000; /* Black heading */
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .text-highlight {
    color: #9acb32; /* Lime green */
  }

  .sub-heading {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #333;
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }
  
  .intro-text {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: #555;
    margin: 0;
  }
  
  .architecture-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }
  
  .architecture-item {
    display: flex;
    gap: 2.5rem;
    padding: 3rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
    
    &:first-child {
      padding-top: 0;
    }
    
    &:last-child {
      border-bottom: none;
